payload.description:
scripts/split-btc-self-test.sh drives btc.split through the real runner offscreen, with env hooks (MUSTER_AUTOSPLIT_CHAIN, MUSTER_AUTOPAYSPLIT). Nobody has looked at the Bitcoin split on a display.

Use the Xvfb + xdotool recipe in docs/labbook/qml-errors-are-invisible-to-nix-build.md against a regtest node (infra/bitcoind/regtest.sh) and check:
- the composer takes a total in BTC and shows exact satoshis;
- the dust refusal (a share below 546 sat) reads clearly;
- payTo shows as a regtest bech32 address;
- the card's Pay my share and Mark received buttons, and the 8-decimal amounts;
- a fiat-quoted BTC split's quote line.

Same pass as exo-a90.13 did for evm.split + lez.split.
